  "note": "Borough elections, 15 January 1931, held under the revised system of an annual quota. Four members were returned for each ward from a single poll, one of whom the council afterwards recognised as the ward's alderman. W. J. Bradley was the ward's alderman; the councillors in order of priority were Johnston-Kee, Thornton and M'Cullagh. A whole-council election: the register (\"Register of Elections of Alderman & Councillors ... held on 15th January 1931\", PRONI LA/20/1/DA/1; Keep note \"LA/20/1/DA/1 Part 2\", #11-#14) marks the member at the top of the poll in each ward, here William John Bradley (548), \"A\": he became the ward's alderman, to retire in 1934, and the other three councillors."
